1
00:00:00,777 --> 00:00:09,157
I found myself lost and alone on this journey

2
00:00:09,157 --> 00:00:17,497
Though my heart wandered far and wide, I could move not an inch

3
00:00:17,497 --> 00:00:22,587
But now I can depart for any distant land

4
00:00:22,587 --> 00:00:25,717
But now I can depart for any distant land

5
00:00:25,717 --> 00:00:28,757
Now that we've met on this road

6
00:00:28,757 --> 00:00:34,557
Now that we've met on this road

7
00:00:35,057 --> 00:00:42,397
Even the unfamiliar songs of travelers

8
00:00:42,397 --> 00:00:53,157
Can spark nostalgia in me when I'm with you

9
00:00:53,157 --> 00:00:57,037
If the world we dreamed of exists somewhere,

10
00:00:57,037 --> 00:01:01,417
If the world we dreamed of exists somewhere,

11
00:01:01,417 --> 00:01:09,847
Then let's go search for it beyond the wind

12
00:01:09,847 --> 00:01:13,807
Through chilling dawns,

13
00:01:13,807 --> 00:01:18,227
Through arid noons,

14
00:01:18,227 --> 00:01:22,187
Through shivering nights,

15
00:01:22,187 --> 00:01:28,197
Let's go see what lies at the end

16
00:01:52,507 --> 00:01:57,517
Wolf and a Lovers' Quarrel

17
00:02:06,647 --> 00:02:08,817
W-Wolf?

18
00:02:08,817 --> 00:02:13,207
If that's true, there's no mistaking their threat here.

19
00:02:13,207 --> 00:02:16,317
"If you don't want your partner to be taken to the Church,

20
00:02:16,317 --> 00:02:18,617
keep quiet until we've finished our business."

21
00:02:19,997 --> 00:02:23,697
But there's no guarantee they won't turn her over to the Church anyway.

22
00:02:24,547 --> 00:02:29,837
We've already invested heavily in Trenni silver by this point, too.

23
00:02:29,837 --> 00:02:31,967
If we back off, we'll suffer huge losses.

24
00:02:32,337 --> 00:02:33,507
We have to strike first!

25
00:02:34,557 --> 00:02:38,037
Let's assume we rescue your partner and take her into asylum here.

26
00:02:38,497 --> 00:02:41,617
If they report us and the Church searches this building,

27
00:02:41,617 --> 00:02:44,767
we'll have no choice but to be as obedient sheep.

28
00:02:45,567 --> 00:02:48,397
She can't hide as long as she's in this city.

29
00:02:48,737 --> 00:02:50,407
We can leave town together.

30
00:02:51,027 --> 00:02:53,947
You'll be caught unless you're extremely lucky.

31
00:02:53,947 --> 00:02:57,407
If that happens, you might be taken to a different town and face persecution.

32
00:02:57,827 --> 00:02:59,907
There would be nothing we could do in that case.

33
00:03:00,787 --> 00:03:05,017
There's no way we can pay them off,
considering how much potential profit is at stake.

34
00:03:06,337 --> 00:03:08,917
If only we had a card to play against them.

35
00:03:08,917 --> 00:03:10,457
There is something.

36
00:03:12,757 --> 00:03:18,797
My company could take the initiative and tell the Church that Medio Trading has your companion.

37
00:03:19,467 --> 00:03:22,637
But if we do, you'll have a problem, right?

38
00:03:22,637 --> 00:03:25,517
You might even give damaging testimony against us.

39
00:03:26,357 --> 00:03:27,817
Without a doubt, I would.

40
00:03:29,567 --> 00:03:31,927
The main point of the scheme

41
00:03:31,927 --> 00:03:35,027
is to receive special rights from the king of Trenni, isn't it?

42
00:03:36,197 --> 00:03:37,997
According to our reports,

43
00:03:37,997 --> 00:03:41,037
the Royal Family is in dire financial straits.

44
00:03:41,037 --> 00:03:42,667
I bet they are.

45
00:03:43,367 --> 00:03:47,207
That's evident from the fact that they're planning to melt the currency in circulation

46
00:03:47,207 --> 00:03:50,957
and decrease its silver content to issue a larger volume of coins.

47
00:03:50,957 --> 00:03:55,667
If ten coins become thirteen, that's a profit of three coins.

48
00:03:56,757 --> 00:03:58,617
They'll instantly raise funds,

49
00:03:58,617 --> 00:04:03,437
but the country's reputation will fall under scrutiny and hurt them in the long term.

50
00:04:04,017 --> 00:04:09,477
For the Trenni Royal Family to do this anyway proves that they're in financial trouble.

51
00:04:10,477 --> 00:04:13,147
That's why, depending on how the negotiation goes,

52
00:04:13,147 --> 00:04:19,117
mining rights, minting rights, tariff rights, and market administration rights are just a sample

53
00:04:19,117 --> 00:04:21,067
of what the Royal Family may grant for our coins.

54
00:04:21,657 --> 00:04:22,907
It's exactly as you say.

55
00:04:22,907 --> 00:04:24,997
How does this sound?

56
00:04:26,327 --> 00:04:28,417
Before Medio presses charges,

57
00:04:28,417 --> 00:04:31,207
finish negotiating with the Royal Family,

58
00:04:31,207 --> 00:04:33,917
and use the rights as a bargaining chip.

59
00:04:35,837 --> 00:04:38,727
I'm sure her value is insignificant compared to those privileges.

60
00:04:39,657 --> 00:04:41,347
Are you saying we should sell the rights?

61
00:04:41,347 --> 00:04:41,967
Yes.

62
00:04:42,597 --> 00:04:46,097
If they believe that they'd be better off buying your rights than crushing you,

63
00:04:46,097 --> 00:04:48,177
Medio Trading will gladly pay the money.

64
00:04:48,937 --> 00:04:52,847
They have a trump card that could send us to the stake.

65
00:04:53,817 --> 00:04:54,477
No.

66
00:04:55,237 --> 00:04:58,117
The last thing the Trenni royals want is trouble with the Church.

67
00:04:58,117 --> 00:05:01,367
They wouldn't want the public to know that they dealt with

68
00:05:01,367 --> 00:05:03,157
a trading company that was sent to the stake.

69
00:05:04,657 --> 00:05:09,747
If we incur the wrath of the Church, they'll eventually turn
against the king, who'll be held responsible by association.

70
00:05:10,287 --> 00:05:14,507
There's no way Medio Trading will prosecute,
since that would bring about the ire of the king.

71
00:05:14,507 --> 00:05:15,757
I see.

72
00:05:15,757 --> 00:05:19,177
But they'd still be reluctant to just back off without a fight.

73
00:05:19,757 --> 00:05:21,917
Even though the only thing they could do is bring us down with them.

74
00:05:22,257 --> 00:05:27,437
And that's where we offer the privileges in exchange for money and your companion.

75
00:05:27,437 --> 00:05:28,767
Exactly.

76
00:05:33,977 --> 00:05:36,237
In theory your plan makes perfect sense.

77
00:05:36,237 --> 00:05:38,817
But there's a significant obstacle to its implementation.

78
00:05:39,617 --> 00:05:41,157
As far as I can guess,

79
00:05:41,157 --> 00:05:44,747
Medio Trading has yet to collect many silver coins.

80
00:05:44,747 --> 00:05:45,777
What makes you say that?

81
00:05:46,287 --> 00:05:49,317
If they had a significant amount of coins,

82
00:05:49,317 --> 00:05:52,247
they would have headed to the Church the moment they captured Holo.

83
00:05:52,247 --> 00:05:55,417
That they chose to forego that option and approach us here

84
00:05:55,417 --> 00:05:57,537
is proof of their lack of confidence.

85
00:05:58,217 --> 00:06:01,507
This plan is one that endeavors to exploit a king.

86
00:06:01,507 --> 00:06:03,557
Medio will have had to keep their coin-gathering quiet.

87
00:06:05,927 --> 00:06:09,057
Mr. Lawrence, what do you propose to do?

88
00:06:09,767 --> 00:06:13,397
We retrieve Holo and I flee with her until you've finalized a deal.

89
00:06:13,687 --> 00:06:14,687
That's preposterous!

90
00:06:15,317 --> 00:06:18,897
Even if I'm unable to escape, I can buy you some time.

91
00:06:19,447 --> 00:06:22,777
Collect as many coins as you can and begin the negotiations.

92
00:06:22,777 --> 00:06:23,987
That's impossible!

93
00:06:24,367 --> 00:06:26,827
In that case, do you plan to tell the Church about Holo?

94
00:06:26,827 --> 00:06:28,907
You'll have to face my testimony if it comes to that.

95
00:06:30,557 --> 00:06:34,337
With your help, I'll be able to evade capture for at least a day or two.

96
00:06:34,337 --> 00:06:37,297
After all, my partner in crime is a wolf spirit.

97
00:06:37,967 --> 00:06:40,127
If her only goal is escape,

98
00:06:40,127 --> 00:06:41,887
and she uses her true abilities,

99
00:06:41,887 --> 00:06:44,047
no human will be able to catch her.

100
00:06:45,967 --> 00:06:47,557
Let me ask you a question.

101
00:06:47,557 --> 00:06:52,057
How long will you need to assemble enough coins to command the king's attention?

102
00:06:57,227 --> 00:07:01,737
If I dispatch someone by horse right now, he should reach Trenni Castle by dusk.

103
00:07:01,737 --> 00:07:03,867
If the negotiations occur immediately,

104
00:07:03,867 --> 00:07:05,737
he'll return by dawn tomorrow.

105
00:07:06,077 --> 00:07:10,747
Right now? You don't even know how many coins you'll be able to collect, do you?

106
00:07:12,077 --> 00:07:14,457
Guesswork has its place in negotiations.

107
00:07:14,457 --> 00:07:17,627
We'll be fine as long as we secure the coins by the time they're due.

108
00:07:18,207 --> 00:07:21,627
Can you reach a quick settlement with a king?

109
00:07:23,177 --> 00:07:27,677
Any deal can be finalized promptly if we put our minds to it.

110
00:07:29,267 --> 00:07:32,437
In that case, do you know where Holo is?

111
00:07:33,597 --> 00:07:36,517
We are Milone Trading, you know.

112
00:07:37,607 --> 00:07:42,657
Ambush of our employees and arson of our facilities

113
00:07:40,357 --> 00:07:41,317
Hey.

114
00:07:42,657 --> 00:07:44,487
are facts of daily life for us.

115
00:07:43,527 --> 00:07:44,487
See you around.

116
00:07:45,157 --> 00:07:47,697
We have contingencies for any emergency.

117
00:07:47,697 --> 00:07:50,247
We do have one rival, though.

118
00:07:50,247 --> 00:07:51,287
Is it the Church?

119
00:07:51,287 --> 00:07:52,827
Correct.

120
00:07:52,827 --> 00:07:57,087
They visit more towns and countries than we do,

121
00:07:57,087 --> 00:08:00,337
and they're surprisingly well-prepared for crisis.

122
00:08:00,337 --> 00:08:06,847
Should the Church launch a search in earnest, you must not run without thinking. Stay hidden in one place.

123
00:08:09,427 --> 00:08:14,977
To tell you the truth, I would have liked to have known who
was backing Medio Trading before we started negotiations.

124
00:08:14,977 --> 00:08:20,847
Then we would know where their funds were coming from
and might even be able to convince them to fund us instead.

125
00:08:22,187 --> 00:08:23,857
Yes, it's not ideal.

126
00:08:23,857 --> 00:08:26,407
I pray for your safety and success.

127
00:08:27,157 --> 00:08:29,117
Your hopes will be met in full.

128
00:08:30,037 --> 00:08:31,947
Oh, that's right.

129
00:08:31,947 --> 00:08:33,997
The passwords are Pireon and Numai.

130
00:08:35,037 --> 00:08:36,457
Two great gold coins, then.

131
00:08:36,827 --> 00:08:38,457
It seemed auspicious.

132
00:08:39,087 --> 00:08:42,917
Once I'm underground, I should touch the right-hand wall and move forward.

133
00:08:42,917 --> 00:08:43,467
Correct?

134
00:08:43,467 --> 00:08:44,337
Yes.

135
00:08:44,337 --> 00:08:46,887
When you hit a wall, you've reached your destination.

136
00:08:50,537 --> 00:08:52,467
Holo will be inside the storage room above.

137
00:08:53,267 --> 00:08:57,977
Your retrieval of the hostage will occur as soon as the bell signals that the market is open.

138
00:08:59,017 --> 00:09:00,227
If everything goes smoothly,

139
00:09:00,227 --> 00:09:03,057
the hatch above the path will open and your partner will descend.

140
00:09:03,647 --> 00:09:05,647
Should you hear the word "Rahhe,"

141
00:09:05,647 --> 00:09:07,817
please wait for an escort to arrive.

142
00:09:09,277 --> 00:09:13,077
If you hear Perouso, make your escape together along the planned route at once.

143
00:09:13,537 --> 00:09:15,077
Rahhe and Perouso.

144
00:09:15,657 --> 00:09:17,457
Prosperity and famine, huh?

145
00:09:17,457 --> 00:09:19,167
Simple to remember, isn't it?

146
00:09:19,167 --> 00:09:20,037
Very.

147
00:09:22,877 --> 00:09:24,207
It's almost time.

148
00:09:29,217 --> 00:09:30,957
You idiot! Watch out!

149
00:09:30,957 --> 00:09:32,177
Sorry.

150
00:09:39,807 --> 00:09:41,977
Go, quickly.

151
00:09:58,577 --> 00:10:00,667
I didn't expect them to be so prepared.

152
00:10:03,627 --> 00:10:06,587
I've heard tell of the Church digging graves as a pretense

153
00:10:06,587 --> 00:10:11,007
to construct underground routes for spying on heretics and evading taxes.

154
00:10:15,637 --> 00:10:16,927
This is it.

155
00:10:34,227 --> 00:10:35,907
Follow me. We're moving.

156
00:11:04,727 --> 00:11:08,277
I hope they don't have to resort to blades or clubs.

157
00:11:13,367 --> 00:11:14,327
Damn.

158
00:11:14,327 --> 00:11:16,447
Why am I trembling?

159
00:11:25,087 --> 00:11:26,247
They're late.

160
00:11:27,087 --> 00:11:27,707
Don't tell me...

161
00:11:43,227 --> 00:11:43,897
Rahhe.

162
00:11:46,437 --> 00:11:47,727
Rahhe.

163
00:11:49,187 --> 00:11:49,857
Numai.

164
00:11:50,687 --> 00:11:51,567
Pireon.

165
00:12:00,327 --> 00:12:01,037
Holo!

166
00:12:02,037 --> 00:12:05,327
I'm supposed to carry this so people will think we're thieves, right?

167
00:12:08,587 --> 00:12:10,007
Now, quick!

168
00:12:10,377 --> 00:12:12,917
I can't come down if you're in the way.

169
00:12:14,087 --> 00:12:15,507
Come on, hurry!

170
00:12:21,307 --> 00:12:24,307
What are you staring at? This is yours.

171
00:12:24,307 --> 00:12:25,517
Hold this and get going.

172
00:12:36,527 --> 00:12:37,657
Yes?

173
00:13:13,527 --> 00:13:14,607
Pireon.

174
00:13:15,197 --> 00:13:16,147
Numai.

175
00:13:21,447 --> 00:13:22,827
Looks like you made it safely.

176
00:13:25,037 --> 00:13:27,787
Life in business is full of surprises.

177
00:13:30,627 --> 00:13:31,877
Our guide is down there.

178
00:13:32,547 --> 00:13:36,377
He'll remove the ladder and exit another way.

179
00:13:37,717 --> 00:13:41,797
He'll then leave town once he informs his contacts about Medio's movements.

180
00:13:42,217 --> 00:13:43,467
You're rather prepared.

181
00:13:45,597 --> 00:13:47,137
Best of luck.

182
00:13:49,687 --> 00:13:50,767
Thanks.

183
00:13:58,277 --> 00:13:59,227
I'm relieved you're unharmed.

184
00:14:00,157 --> 00:14:02,027
You're relieved to see I'm unharmed?

185
00:14:02,577 --> 00:14:03,407
Yeah.

186
00:14:04,697 --> 00:14:06,577
Say my name!

187
00:14:06,577 --> 00:14:08,317
Holo... right?

188
00:14:08,327 --> 00:14:09,697
Holo, the wise wolf!

189
00:14:10,417 --> 00:14:11,877
R-Right.

190
00:14:12,457 --> 00:14:18,217
I can remember every single person who ever shamed me in my life.

191
00:14:18,717 --> 00:14:21,797
I must add a new name to that list.

192
00:14:21,797 --> 00:14:23,087
Yours!

193
00:14:23,847 --> 00:14:24,717
I don't...

194
00:14:24,717 --> 00:14:28,847
Didn't I tell you to come and save me?

195
00:14:28,847 --> 00:14:29,937
Y-Yeah.

196
00:14:29,937 --> 00:14:34,727
I... I was so convinced that <i>you</i> came, and...

197
00:14:35,897 --> 00:14:37,557
I feel angry just thinking about it!

198
00:14:38,237 --> 00:14:40,067
Don't tell me you...

199
00:14:41,197 --> 00:14:45,447
You're a male, aren't you? Shouldn't you have been at the forefront, fighting tooth and nail?

200
00:14:45,447 --> 00:14:47,707
But you hid in a hole in the ground.

201
00:14:47,707 --> 00:14:49,917
You let me make a fool of myself!

202
00:14:52,037 --> 00:14:53,627
At least you're safe.

203
00:15:06,307 --> 00:15:07,467
I'm glad you're all right.

204
00:15:09,517 --> 00:15:13,607
I can't die as long as you hold on to the wheat.

205
00:15:15,727 --> 00:15:19,567
Human males are easy prey since I'm so cute.

206
00:15:19,567 --> 00:15:23,867
Yet, not one of my opponents were fit to be my mate.

207
00:15:24,737 --> 00:15:27,327
They turned pale in fear as soon as I said,

208
00:15:27,327 --> 00:15:29,747
"I'll sever your private parts if you so much as touch me."

209
00:15:30,827 --> 00:15:31,827
Hey, now.

210
00:15:33,787 --> 00:15:34,667
But...

211
00:15:36,227 --> 00:15:39,167
That's when <i>she</i> appeared before me.

212
00:15:41,837 --> 00:15:46,007
Can you guess who was among those who captured me?

213
00:15:46,507 --> 00:15:48,097
Who?

214
00:15:48,097 --> 00:15:49,137
Chloe.

215
00:15:50,177 --> 00:15:51,807
The girl from Pasloei Village.

216
00:15:57,067 --> 00:16:00,357
She apparently heard my name from Zheren.

217
00:16:05,567 --> 00:16:06,527
Did you speak with her?

218
00:16:07,577 --> 00:16:10,287
I thought you were simply a fairy tale.

219
00:16:11,117 --> 00:16:12,787
Only for a moment.

220
00:16:13,247 --> 00:16:20,417
"A wolf spirit lives within the village's wheat fields and determines the quality of the harvest on a whim."

221
00:16:20,417 --> 00:16:25,587
I don't know how many years it's been since I settled down in that land.

222
00:16:26,387 --> 00:16:29,177
Maybe as many as there are hairs on my tail.

223
00:16:29,177 --> 00:16:31,017
I'm Holo, the wise wolf.

224
00:16:31,017 --> 00:16:37,227
In order to provide the greatest harvest, I let the soil rest on occasion by producing a poor yield.

225
00:16:38,187 --> 00:16:40,397
That was all part of managing the land.

226
00:16:40,397 --> 00:16:43,987
Wheat would have grown better there than anywhere else.

227
00:16:44,737 --> 00:16:49,607
It's true that the people of the village worshipped me as their god of harvest,

228
00:16:49,607 --> 00:16:53,567
but not out of respect. It was more akin to a desire to control.

229
00:16:53,997 --> 00:16:57,877
The person who reaps the last stalk of wheat is locked away.

230
00:17:00,797 --> 00:17:03,167
Do you know what Chloe said to me?

231
00:17:04,257 --> 00:17:10,847
She said she heard my name from Zheren, and it made her wonder if I was <i>her</i> Holo.

232
00:17:13,557 --> 00:17:15,717
I... I...

233
00:17:18,187 --> 00:17:20,977
I was happy, as shameful as that sounds.

234
00:17:23,397 --> 00:17:26,947
However, she didn't stop there.

235
00:17:27,947 --> 00:17:32,287
Gone are the days of having to court your favor.

236
00:17:32,287 --> 00:17:36,497
There's no need to gnash our teeth at your fickle nature anymore.

237
00:17:39,457 --> 00:17:44,257
I'll send you to the Church and bid farewell to all those dated traditions.

238
00:17:57,437 --> 00:18:00,557
I... I...

239
00:18:01,437 --> 00:18:03,187
I couldn't stand it!

240
00:18:20,417 --> 00:18:23,047
Well, look at it a different way.

241
00:18:27,837 --> 00:18:31,847
You'll have to leave the wheatfields in order to return to the north.

242
00:18:32,637 --> 00:18:36,847
If they say you won't be missed, blind them with the dust cloud you leave.

243
00:18:37,557 --> 00:18:39,897
It'll be a cleaner break that way.

244
00:18:39,897 --> 00:18:42,477
You won't be leaving quietly, though.

245
00:18:43,687 --> 00:18:46,857
I, I mean we, are merchants.

246
00:18:46,857 --> 00:18:48,067
We profit, we triumph.

247
00:18:48,947 --> 00:18:51,697
We'll laugh when we make money,

248
00:18:51,697 --> 00:18:53,827
and cry when we don't have a cent.

249
00:18:57,447 --> 00:19:00,537
And I think we'll end up laughing.

250
00:19:03,667 --> 00:19:05,417
I feel better.

251
00:19:06,417 --> 00:19:07,417
Well...

252
00:19:09,087 --> 00:19:12,257
I haven't had a proper conversation in hundreds of years.

253
00:19:12,257 --> 00:19:14,047
My emotions are far too fragile.

254
00:19:14,887 --> 00:19:17,637
This is the second time I've cried in front of you,

255
00:19:17,637 --> 00:19:20,227
but I would have done so even had <i>you</i> not been here.

256
00:19:20,227 --> 00:19:21,797
Do you understand what I'm saying?

257
00:19:22,267 --> 00:19:24,267
Don't get the wrong idea?

258
00:19:24,267 --> 00:19:25,107
Right.

259
00:19:25,567 --> 00:19:28,057
I only brought you along to help me make money, anyway.

260
00:19:28,897 --> 00:19:33,777
Our job is to run for as long as we can until Milone Trading negotiates a deal.

261
00:19:34,237 --> 00:19:38,247
Having someone crying and carrying on in the middle of that is just a burden.

262
00:19:38,247 --> 00:19:41,457
So regardless of who was crying in front of me, I'd...

263
00:19:43,707 --> 00:19:45,847
Hey, that isn't fair.

264
00:19:45,847 --> 00:19:48,257
Mm-hm. A female's privilege.

265
00:19:49,667 --> 00:19:51,467
We've arrived.

266
00:19:52,797 --> 00:19:55,597
Have you run out of things to say?

267
00:19:55,597 --> 00:19:56,217
No.

268
00:19:58,307 --> 00:20:02,477
The man behind Medio Trading is Count Ehrendott.

269
00:20:02,477 --> 00:20:07,017
The merchant within the Count's manor in charge of
brokering wheat is responsible for collecting the silver coins.

270
00:20:08,317 --> 00:20:10,527
Report this to Marlheit.

271
00:20:10,937 --> 00:20:12,067
Consider it done.

272
00:20:12,777 --> 00:20:18,287
It's true, then, that those who bring talk of profit are rather odd.

273
00:20:18,287 --> 00:20:19,607
What, you mean my ears?

274
00:20:20,907 --> 00:20:25,117
Looking at you two makes me want to live the life of a traveling merchant again.

275
00:20:25,627 --> 00:20:27,087
I advise against it.

276
00:20:30,797 --> 00:20:33,007
You'll end up stuck with someone like her.

277
00:20:33,007 --> 00:20:38,257
Nothing wrong with that. The seat of a wagon is too big for one person anyway.

278
00:20:42,097 --> 00:20:45,517
Surely I'm the unfortunate one,
to be picked up by the likes of you!

279
00:20:47,397 --> 00:20:49,777
You're too clever by half.

280
00:20:49,777 --> 00:20:52,017
That's what makes me so charming.

281
00:20:54,567 --> 00:20:56,767
Well, that much is true.

282
00:21:01,787 --> 00:21:03,457
I'm so happy you said that.

283
00:21:05,997 --> 00:21:08,667
You really are an adorable boy.

284
00:21:10,127 --> 00:21:11,087
Geez.

285
00:23:40,847 --> 00:23:44,157
<i>Next Episode: "Wolf and a Silent Farewell".</i>

286
00:23:45,867 --> 00:23:48,787
<i>Next Episode: "Wolf and a Silent Farewell".</i>

